  "notes": "{緩|ゆる}める is a transitive ichidan verb. The intransitive counterpart is {緩|ゆる}む (to become loose).\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{緩|ゆる}めている indicates the ongoing action of loosening, or a state where something has been loosened.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- [object]を{緩|ゆる}める (to loosen something)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ネクタイを{緩|ゆる}める (to loosen a necktie)\n- {速度|そくど}を{緩|ゆる}める (to reduce speed)\n- {規制|きせい}を{緩|ゆる}める (to relax regulations)\n- {気|き}を{緩|ゆる}める (to let one's guard down)\n- {手綱|たづな}を{緩|ゆる}める (to slacken the reins)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {緩|ゆる}める: to loosen, to relax (general)\n- {弛|ゆる}める: to slacken (variant kanji, same reading)\n- {解|ほど}く: to untie, to undo (completely releasing a knot)",
